      "cuttlefish": "Cuttlefish",
      "cuttlefish_and_squid_catch_fish_using_": "Cuttlefish and squid catch fish using a \"tentacle strike\" — two specialized feeding tentacles fire forward in <40ms, faster than the fish's startle response.",
      "cuttlefish_appear_to_have_number_sense": "Cuttlefish appear to have number sense — they can choose the larger of two prey items when offered.",
      "cuttlefish_are_unique_among_cephalopod": "Cuttlefish are unique among cephalopods in that they STALK their prey on the bottom — using their chromatophore patterns to match substrate as they approach.",
      "cuttlefish_can_predict_the_trajectory_": "Cuttlefish can predict the trajectory of moving prey — they fire their feeding tentacles to the projected position, not where the prey currently is.",
      "cuttlefish_can_produce_over_30_distinc": "Cuttlefish can produce over 30 distinct body-pattern combinations using their chromatophores + iridophores + leucophores + papillae. Each is suited to a particular environmental context.",
      "cuttlefish_display_intense_zebra_patte": "Cuttlefish display \"intense zebra\" patterns on one side of the body (facing rival males) and a different pattern on the other side (facing female) — using each body half for different audience.",
      "cuttlefish_exert_self_control_in_a_del": "Cuttlefish exert self-control in a delay of gratification task",
      "cuttlefish_exhibit_lateralized_display": "Cuttlefish exhibit LATERALIZED displays — showing different patterns on the left + right sides of the body to convey different information to different audiences simultaneously.",
      "cuttlefish_form_internal_shell_becomes": "Cuttlefish form: internal shell becomes a flat porous calcium structure (the cuttlebone) for buoyancy control.",
      "cuttlefish_have_a_porous_internal_shel": "Cuttlefish have a porous internal shell (cuttlebone) made of aragonite. They control buoyancy by adjusting the gas-to-liquid ratio in each chamber.",
      "cuttlefish_ink_sepia_melanin_has_been_": "Cuttlefish ink (Sepia melanin) has been used in art + writing for centuries. It's the source of the brown \"sepia\" tone of old photographs.",
      "cuttlefish_lateralize_their_displays_u": "Cuttlefish lateralize their displays — using one side of the body for one audience and the other side for another. A \"two-faced\" tactic.",
      "cuttlefish_often_hover_stationary_just": "Cuttlefish often hover stationary just above the substrate, matching color. Watch for the distinctive flat oval body shape + visible W-shaped pupils — different from octopus.",
      "cuttlefish_papillae_3d_skin_bumps_can_": "Cuttlefish papillae (3D skin bumps) can persist for hours after the rest of the skin pattern has shifted — texture is locked in longer than color.",
      "cuttlefish_remember_when_and_where_spe": "Cuttlefish remember WHEN AND WHERE specific events occurred — a form of episodic-like memory documented by Schnell et al. (2021).",
      "cuttlefish_self_control_test": "Cuttlefish self-control test",
      "cuttlefish_show_preference_for_higher_": "Cuttlefish show preference for HIGHER-QUALITY food + will wait for it — a \"marshmallow test\" demonstration of self-control.",
      "cuttlefish_squid_feeding_tentacles_fir": "Cuttlefish + squid feeding tentacles fire forward at speeds reaching 10 m/s — among the fastest accelerations in the animal kingdom. The tentacles strike + retract in <40 ms.",
      "cuttlefish_stalking_strategy_involves_": "Cuttlefish stalking strategy involves a slow approach with arms tucked + chromatophore pattern matched to substrate. They wait until they're within 1 body-length before firing tentacles.",
      "cuttlefish_use_hypnotic_display_passin": "Cuttlefish use HYPNOTIC DISPLAY (\"passing cloud\") to mesmerize prey before tentacle strike. Cause-and-effect of the display is documented in lab + field — prey freeze for 1-2 seconds.",
      "cuttlefish_use_polarization_sensitivit": "Cuttlefish use polarization sensitivity in predation on silvery fish",
      "cuttlefish_use_polarization_sensitivit_2": "Cuttlefish use polarization sensitivity in predation on silvery fish",
      "cuttlefish_use_polarization_vision_to_": "Cuttlefish use POLARIZATION VISION to detect transparent prey — fish that are invisible to most predators are visible to cuttlefish polarization-sensitive eyes.",
      "cuttlefish_use_two_long_feeding_tentac": "Cuttlefish use TWO long feeding tentacles that fire forward in <40 ms — faster than fish startle reflexes.",
      "cuttlefish_use_visual_cues_to_control_": "Cuttlefish use visual cues to control three-dimensional skin papillae for camouflage",
      "cuttlefish_various": "Cuttlefish (various)",
