      "pelagic_predator_from_the_eastern_paci": "Pelagic predator from the Eastern Pacific. Up to 2 m mantle length. Hunts in schools of 20-1200 individuals. Aggressive — Mexican fishermen call them diablos rojos (\"red devils\") because of their threat displays. Skin chromatophores flash red/white at 2-4 Hz when hunting, possibly a signal to schoolmates. Massive jet speed, but extremely high stamina cost — manage your jet carefully or starve. Active hunter, not an ambusher.",
