      "trait_divergence_milestone_30": "teaching milestone (30%)",
      "trait_divergence_milestone_limit": "A geographic barrier splits an ancestral population. Each half evolves under its own pressure. This simplified model marks a teaching milestone when one trait's overlap proxy falls below 30%. Real speciation requires evidence of independently evolving lineages and reproductive isolation or other species criteria; this activity does not test mating.",
      "trait_divergence_model": "Trait Divergence Model",
      "trait_divergence_model_2": "Trait Divergence Model",
      "trait_divergence_model_3": "Trait Divergence Model",
      "trait_divergence_model_overview": "A geographic barrier separates two teaching populations and selection shifts one quantitative trait on each side. The overlap score is a visualization of trait divergence, not a measurement of reproductive isolation or proof of separate species.",
      "trait_means_overlap_proxy_over_time": "Trait Means + Overlap Proxy Over Time",
