      "tell_the_patron_the_deadline_must_slip": "Tell the patron the deadline must slip by a week. Explain why.",
      "the_1457_mainz_psalter_fust_sch_ffer_u": "The 1457 Mainz Psalter (Fust & Schöffer) used a complicated two-color printing technique: the body type in black, the large initial capitals printed in red and blue on the same impression. This required printing each page through the press in multiple passes with the type inked in different colors. Most scholars consider it among the most beautifully printed books ever made.",
      "the_95_theses_2": "The 95 Theses",
      "the_aldine_dolphin_and_anchor_was_so_h": "The Aldine dolphin-and-anchor was so heavily pirated that Aldus published a guide to spotting fakes.",
      "the_apprentice_agrees": "The apprentice agrees:",
      "the_closing_two_paragraphs_shift_from_": "The closing two paragraphs shift from work to home. What does Konrad seem to want most from his mother's reply, and how is that different from what an apprentice in 2026 might want from a parent?",
      "the_compositor_a_journeyman_three_year": "The compositor — a journeyman three years your senior — drops a galley. The type \"falls in pi\" (becomes a jumbled pile). It will take an hour to sort. He glances at you. He saw you watching. He could blame you.",
      "the_estienne_family": "The Estienne family",
      "the_first_newspaper_printed_in_what_wo": ", the first newspaper printed in what would become Maine. They set up a press in Falmouth (now Portland) thirty-five years before Maine statehood, when Maine was still the District of Maine inside Massachusetts. Their press ran from a small shop on Fore Street.",
      "the_food_is_plain_but_enough_the_maste": "The food is plain but enough. The Master's wife sees that I have bread and broth in the morning and meat at supper. I sleep on a straw mattress with the other apprentice in the loft above the press room. He is from Cologne and snores like a stuck pig.",
      "the_interest_accrues_whether_you_finis": "“The interest accrues whether you finish the Bible or not. Pay, or the press is mine.”",
      "the_master_agrees": "The Master agrees:",
      "the_master_sends_you_to_fetch_oil_base": "The master sends you to fetch oil-based ink from the cellar. You realize the shop has only enough for half a day. Telling him will mean blame for not noticing earlier. Saying nothing means the press stops at midday.",
      "the_original_writing_will_atrophy_memo": "The original \"writing will atrophy memory\" argument that print critics inherited.",
      "the_platen_has_a_slight_warp_from_yest": "The platen has a slight warp from yesterday's heat. Re-leveling takes 90 minutes. Pressing through means slightly uneven impressions all morning.",
      "the_press": "The press",
      "the_shop_carries_my_husband_s_name_the": "“The shop carries my husband’s name. The work carries mine.”",
      "the_shop_closes_at_sunset_another_appr": "The shop closes at sunset. Another apprentice asks if you would help him learn the letter positions in the type case (he is behind). Helping him means staying late. The master prefers apprentices rest so they work fresh tomorrow.",
      "these_are_not_invented_or_exaggerated_": "These are not invented or exaggerated. Each was a genuine, documented concern voiced by someone in the 1450-1600 period. The voice attribution names the actual source where the concern was raised.",
      "these_quotes_are_not_historical_transc": "These quotes are NOT historical transcripts — imagined paraphrases in the voice each figure is documented to have used. Pick the most likely speaker.",
      "thomas_b_wait_benjamin_titcomb": "Thomas B. Wait & Benjamin Titcomb",
      "three_orders_arrive_this_morning_a_a_b": "Three orders arrive this morning. (A) A Bible commission — prestigious, low margin, 6 months of work. (B) An almanac — quick, mass-market, mid margin. (C) A heretical pamphlet — high margin, but printing it could mean Church penalties or worse.",
      "title_size": "Title size: ",
      "to_deal_with_the_apprentice_in_good_fa": ". To deal with the apprentice in good faith and not to put him to work beneath the trade.",
      "to_instruct_the_apprentice_in_casting_": " to instruct the apprentice in casting type, setting type, the working of the press, the mixing of ink, and the keeping of a shop. To furnish ",
      "to_serve_faithfully_day_and_night_to_k": " to serve faithfully day and night, to keep the secrets of the trade and not reveal them to any rival shop, to ",
      "to_take_no_wife_during_the_term_to_obe": ", to take no wife during the term, to obey the Master and his household in all lawful things, and not to absent himself from service without leave.",
      "today_i_dropped_a_tray_not_the_type_th": "Today I dropped a tray. Not the type, thank God, but the wooden tray underneath it. The journeyman pressman did not see, and Master Konrad pretended not to. I will be more careful. The trade is full of dangers I had not thought of when we spoke before I left home: the lead, the boiling oil for the ink, the heavy quoins that can crush a finger. Already I have a small burn on my left hand from the casting room. It is healing.",
      "tom_standage_writing_on_the_wall_socia": "Tom Standage, \"Writing on the Wall: Social Media in the First 2,000 Years\" (2013)",
      "top_down_floor_plan_of_a_1455_mainz_pr": "Top-down floor plan of a 1455 Mainz print shop",
      "train_another_apprentice_long_term_cap": "Train another apprentice — long-term capacity.",
      "try_to_clean_the_smudge_yourself_with_": "Try to clean the smudge yourself with a damp cloth.",
